      "footnotes": [],
      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Entries such as \"(First instalment 1915)\" and \"( ,, ,, 1919)\" are printed once spanning the two columns \"Charge for 1911\" and \"Principal paid off\"; repeated in both cells here.",
        "1898 Belgian Loan: \"Redeemed 1908\" printed in the Charge for 1911 column.",
        "1905 Hongkong Government Loan: Principal outstanding printed \"£1,100,00\" (one digit short of the principal £1,100,000); transcribed as printed.",
        "1907 Franco-Belgian Supplementary Loan to 1903: its figures (£640,000 ... 1932 ... £640,000) are printed on the line of the first line of the following entry (1907 British and Chinese Corporation Canton-Kowloon Railway), whose own figures are on its second line; assigned to the Franco-Belgian row by layout.",
        "Price of Issue \"98¾\" for the 1908 and 1909 Tientsin-Pukow loans: the fraction is very small; read as ¾.",
        "Heading figure £32,545,800 = total principal outstanding: the outstanding column sums to £31,555,800 taking \"£1,100,00\" as printed (i.e. 110,000) — does NOT reconcile as printed (diff 990,000); it would reconcile exactly if that cell were £1,100,000. Principal amounts (£ only, excluding the Tls. 5,000,000 loan) sum to £37,448,300."
      ],
